=¢ko¬ì˜¤ë…¸ë£¨ì•„¢zh¬å¥¥è¯ºé²ç“¦¦quests‘…¢idÎ␀q¤name„¢en´A Requiem for Heroes¢jaµè‹±é›„ã¸ã®éŽ®é­‚æ­Œ¢de²Requiem der Helden¢frºUn requiem pour les hÃ©ros¤icon´/i/071000/071201.png§rewards‘‚¢idÍmA¦amount¦banner´/i/100000/100840.png§1018143Œ¥patch ¢id§1018143¢en¨Gaetelle¢ja¬ã‚¬ã‚¨ãƒ†ãƒ«¢de¨Gaetelle¢fr¨Gaetelle¥title„¢en ¢ja ¢de ¢fr ¬defaultTalks‘’Ù¯Ever since the inconsistencies in Ishgard's history and the church's teachings were brought to light, I feared it to be the end of an era and, by extension, the scholasticate.Ùº[UNHANDLED 0x2C], I cannot tell you how wrong I was. If anything, our fine establishment flourished in the aftermath and, with the help of our dedicated students, will continue to do so.¨position…¦zoneidÍ	!£mapÌÜ¡xË@Që…¸R¡yË@\(õÂ¡z␀¢ko©ê°€ì—í…”¢zh¬åŠ åŸƒæ³°å‹’¦quests§1018144Œ¥patch ¢id§1018144¢enªTheomocent¢ja¯ãƒ†ã‚ªãƒ¢ã‚µãƒ³¢deªTheomocent¢frªTheomocent¥title„¢en ¢ja ¢de ¢fr ¬defaultTalks‘’Ùº[UNHANDLED 0x2C]! How wonderful of you to come visit! We've been working to reform the foundation of our current school system and curriculum and things here have seen great improvement.Ù£Every day, I feel as though I'm moving a step closer to achieving my dreams and bringing about the change Father Choisseau had hoped Ishgard would one day embrace.¨position…¦zoneidÍ	!£mapÌÜ¡xË@¸Që…¡yË@=p£×
=¡z␀¢ko¬í…Œì˜¤ëª¨ìƒ¢zh¬ç‰¹å¥¥èŽ«æ¡‘¦quests§1018145Œ¥patch ¢id§1018145¢en¥Leigh¢ja¦ãƒ¬ã‚¤¢de¥Leigh¢fr¥Leigh¥title„¢en ¢ja ¢de ¢fr ¬defaultTalks‘’Ù’[UNHANDLED 0x2C]! How go your adventures? Since I last saw you, I've had a few of my ownâ”€all of which have involved keeping Theo out of trouble.ÙrThe only good thing about having Archombadin around is that he somehow manages to sense trouble before it happens.¨position…¦zoneidÍ	!£mapÌÜ¡xË@áG®zá¡yË@\(õÂ\¡z␀¢ko£ë¦¬¢zh¦é›·ä¼Š¦quests§1018146Œ¥patch ¢id§1018146¢enªCrammevoix¢ja²ã‚¯ãƒ©ãƒ ãƒ´ã‚©ãƒ¯¢deªCrammevoix¢frªCrammevoix¥title„¢en ¢ja ¢de ¢fr ¬defaultTalks‘‘ÚWelcome back, [UNHANDLED 0x2C]! You won't believe how much the scholasticate has changed! The somber atmosphere that hovered over the scholasticate has been replaced by radiant joy and not a single day goes by that these halls aren't filled with the jubilant laughter of seminarians.¨position…¦zoneidÍ	!£mapÌÜ¡x¡yË@Që…¸R¡z␀¢ko¬í¬ëž¨ë¶€ì•„¢zh¬å…‹æ‹‰å§†ç“¦¦quests§1018147Œ¥patch ¢id§1018147¢en§Blaisie¢ja¬ãƒ–ãƒ¬ã‚¸ãƒ¼¢de§Blaisie¢fr§Blaisie¥title„¢en ¢ja ¢de ¢fr ¬defaultTalks‘’ÙƒOh, [UNHANDLED 0x2C], with everyone working so well together to make the scholasticate a better place, Theo has never been happier.ÙoHis smile grows more radiant by the day, and with each passing week I come to loâ€”er, admire him all the more.¨position…¦zoneidÍ	!£mapÌÜ¡xË@=p£×
=¡yË@\(õÂ\¡z␀¢ko©ë¸”ë ˆì§€¢zh©å¸ƒèŽ±è¥¿¦quests§1018148Œ¥patch ¢id§1018148¢enµdespondent seminarian¢jaµãƒ–ãƒ¬ã‚¸ãƒ¼ã®å‹äºº¢de·Freundin[p] von Blaisie¢fr¯amie de Blaisie¥title„¢en ¢ja ¢de ¢fr ¬defaultTalks‘’Ù§Recently, Blaisie and I started talking again. After opening up to her about how much her silence hurt me, we reconnected and now our friendship is stronger than ever!ÙÀ...There's just one teensy problem. You see, Theomocent is completely oblivious to how Blaisie feels about him but she's too shy to admit anything. The two of them are so frustrating to watch!¨position…¦zoneidÍ	!£mapÌÜ¡xË@333333¡yË@…¸Që…¡z␀¢ko³ë¸”ë ˆì§€ì˜ ì¹œêµ¬¢zh²å¸ƒèŽ±è¥¿çš„å‹äºº¦quests§1018149Œ¥patch ¢id§1018149¢en«Archombadin¢ja¸ã‚¢ãƒ«ã‚·ãƒ§ãƒ³ãƒãƒ€ãƒ³¢de«Archombadin¢fr«Archombadin¥title„¢en ¢ja ¢de ¢fr ¬defaultTalks‘’Ù”I paid a visit to Lebrassoir soon after he was escorted off scholasticate grounds by the Temple Knights. He refused to even acknowledge my presence.Ú It will take a great deal of time for me to gain his forgiveness, it seems. <sigh> In the meantime, I shall do what I can to see that the scholasticate's reputation is restored. Together with Theo, I feel we will be able to pave the path toward a brighter future for all seminarians here.¨position…¦zoneidÍ	!£mapÌÜ¡xË@G®záH¡yË@õÂ\(ö¡z␀¢ko¯ì•„ë¥´ìˆŒë°”ëŒ•¢zh¯é˜¿å°”é›„å·´ä¸¹¦quests§1018150Œ¥patch ¢id§1018150¢en°stern seminarian¢ja¸åŽ³æ ¼ãªå…ˆè¼©ç¥žå­¦ç”Ÿ¢de°ernst[a] Student¢fr°Ã©lÃ¨ve austÃ¨re¥title„¢en ¢ja ¢de ¢fr ¬defaultTalks‘’ÚThe history we were taught growing up was all a lie, the priest and mentor I had come to respect the most was a fraud, Lebrassoir was never loyal to the Dzemaels, and now Archombadin and Theomocent are practically joined at the hip... It's as if the world's gone mad!ÙòBut perhaps a little madness was just what I needed, for all these changes have made me realize how narrow-minded and set in my own ways I was. From now on I shall endeavor to be more accommodating and accepting of others' ideas and opinions.¨position…¦zoneidÍ	!£mapÌÜ¡xË@G®záH¡yË@õÂ\(ö¡z␀¢koºì—„ê²©í•œ ì„ ë°° ì‹ í•™ìƒ¢zh²ä¸¥åŽ‰çš„ç¥žå­¦ç”Ÿ¦quests§1018151Œ¥patch ¢id§1018151¢en²sincere seminarian¢ja»ç„¡é‚ªæ°—ãªå¾Œè¼©ç¥žå­¦ç”Ÿ¢de´unbesorgt[a] Student¢fr¯Ã©lÃ¨ve candide¥title„¢en ¢ja ¢de ¢fr ¬defaultTalks‘’ÙLately, one of the seniors who had made it his life's mission to observe and criticize everything I do has become almost cordial.ÙÒWhere before, I would have to endure one-sided lectures, now we have <i>actual</i> conversations. I must say this change has made me more receptive to what he has to say, and every day my respect for him grows.¨position…¦zoneidÍ	!£mapÌÜ¡xË@
