=q¡zË¿„záG®{¢ko¬ìœ„ë¦¬ì•™ì œ¢zh¬äºŽé‡Œæ˜‚çƒ­¦quests‘„¢idÎ␀Æ¤name„¢en¶Reflections in Crystal¢ja¸ã‚¯ãƒªã‚¹ã‚¿ãƒ«ã®æ®‹å…‰¢de´Kristall-Reflexionen¢fr¶RÃ©manences de cristal¤icon´/i/071000/071201.png¦banner´/i/101000/101011.png§1033894Œ¥patchE¢id§1033894¢en¤Ryne¢ja©ãƒªãƒ¼ãƒ³¢de¤Ryne¢fr¤Ryne¥title„¢en ¢ja ¢de ¢fr ¬defaultTalks¨position…¦zoneidÍ—£mapÍ#¡xË@®záG®¡yË@333333¡zË¿„záG®{¢ko£ë¦°¢zh£ç³¦quests‘„¢idÎ␀Æ¤name„¢en¶Reflections in Crystal¢ja¸ã‚¯ãƒªã‚¹ã‚¿ãƒ«ã®æ®‹å…‰¢de´Kristall-Reflexionen¢fr¶RÃ©manences de cristal¤icon´/i/071000/071201.png¦banner´/i/101000/101011.png§1033896Œ¥patchE¢id§1033896¢enªG'raha Tia¢ja¸ã‚°ãƒ»ãƒ©ãƒãƒ»ãƒ†ã‚£ã‚¢¢deªG'raha Tia¢frªG'raha Tia¥title„¢en ¢ja ¢de ¢fr ¬defaultTalks¨position…¦zoneidÍá£mapÌˆ¡xË@™™™™™š¡yË@=p£×
=¡zË¿„záG®{¢ko°ê·¸ë¼í•˜ í‹°ì•„¢zh³å¤Â·æ‹‰å“ˆÂ·æäºš¦quests‘„¢idÎ␀Æ¤name„¢en¶Reflections in Crystal¢ja¸ã‚¯ãƒªã‚¹ã‚¿ãƒ«ã®æ®‹å…‰¢de´Kristall-Reflexionen¢fr¶RÃ©manences de cristal¤icon´/i/071000/071201.png¦banner´/i/101000/101011.png§1033897Œ¥patchE¢id§1033897¢en©Alphinaud¢ja¯ã‚¢ãƒ«ãƒ•ã‚£ãƒŽ¢de©Alphinaud¢fr©Alphinaud¥title„¢en ¢ja ¢de ¢fr ¬defaultTalks‘“ÙŒThanks to your reports, I had known that all was well in the Source, but there is no relief like seeing our comrades again with my own eyes.Ù¦If possible, I should like to thank Estinien in person for the help he lent us while we were away, but it seems he has not been heard from of late. Such is his way...Ù¤Well, until such time as we meet again, I shall ever pray for his well-being, and take the absence of tidings as a good sign. As I do with our friends in the First.¨position…¦zoneidÍá£mapÌˆ¡xË@×
=p£×¡yË@…¸Që…¡z␀¢ko©ì•Œí”¼ë…¸¢zh¬é˜¿å°”è²è¯º¦quests§1033898Œ¥patchE¢id§1033898¢en§Alisaie¢ja¬ã‚¢ãƒªã‚¼ãƒ¼¢de§Alisaie¢fr§Alisaie¥title„¢en ¢ja ¢de ¢fr ¬defaultTalks‘’ÙWhile things are quiet, I think I'll move my body around some more. Need to get it used to the new tricks I learned in the First.ÙªTo that end, I'll round up Hoary and his crew for a spot of sparring. Oh, and G'raha too. In my capacity as his senior, I'm obligated to train him as well, heh heh heh...¨position…¦zoneidÍá£mapÌˆ¡xË@¸Që…¸¡yË@záG®{¡zË¿„záG®{¢ko©ì•Œë¦¬ì œ¢zh©é˜¿èŽ‰å¡ž¦quests§1033899Œ¥patchE¢id§1033899¢en¨Thancred¢ja²ã‚µãƒ³ã‚¯ãƒ¬ãƒƒãƒ‰¢de¨Thancred¢fr¨Thancred¥title„¢en ¢ja ¢de ¢fr ¬defaultTalks‘“ÙYThough only a short time has passed in the Source, for me it has been several long years.Ù'Tis passing strange to see how little has changed here in the Rising Stones. Sometimes I can't help but feel as if I'm dreaming.Ù Then I see the equipment Tataru prepared for us, and it helps to bring me back to reality. Ryne continues her fight in the First, and I must resume my own here.¨position…¦zoneidÍá£mapÌˆ¡xË@333333¡yË@õÂ\(ö¡zË?”záG®{¢ko¬ì‚°í¬ë ˆë“œ¢zh¬æ¡‘å…‹ç‘žå¾·¦quests§1033900Œ¥patchE¢id§1033900¢en¨Y'shtola¢ja²ãƒ¤ãƒ»ã‚·ãƒ¥ãƒˆãƒ©¢de¨Y'shtola¢fr¨Y'shtola¥title„¢en ¢ja ¢de ¢fr ¬defaultTalks‘“Ù¬As you know, in Seeker of the Sun culture, the title tia indicates a male who does not preside over territory. In regards to this, Alphinaud came to me with a consultation.ÙÄThe Crystarium may not be a territory in the traditional sense, he said, but our friend governed it with great leadership nonetheless. As such, would it not be inappropriate to call him â€œTiaâ€?ÙéAs it is by no means disrespectful to omit the title, I told Alphinaud that he is free to do so if he wishes. But I for one intend to call him by his full name. At least until he has decided what he wants for himself in his new life.¨position…¦zoneidÍá£mapÌˆ¡xË@G®záH¡yË@ë…¸Qì¡zË?”záG®{¢ko¬ì•¼ìŠˆí†¨ë¼¢zh®é›…Â·ä¿®ç‰¹æ‹‰¦quests§1033901Œ¥patchE¢id§1033901¢en¨Urianger¢ja²ã‚¦ãƒªã‚¨ãƒ³ã‚¸ã‚§¢de¨Urianger¢fr¨Urianger¥title„¢en ¢ja ¢de ¢fr ¬defaultTalks‘“Ù¢By thine account, the Fourteenth seat of the Convocation was known as Azem. At the title's distinctly familiar ring, mine imagination could not fail but run wild.Ù¸From Azeyma, the Warden, in Eorzea to Azim, the Dawn Father, in the Far East, in nigh every corner of Hydaelyn do those deities revered as personifications of the sun share like names.ÙÄCould they all perhaps trace their origin to the Fourteenth seat, I did muse. Though it may ne'er be proven or otherwise, such a theory, I do believe, lieth firmly within the realm of possibility.¨position…¦zoneidÍá£mapÌˆ¡xË@ÌÌÌÌÌÍ¡yË@¸Që…¸¡zË?”záG®{¢ko¬ìœ„ë¦¬ì•™ì œ¢zh¬äºŽé‡Œæ˜‚çƒ­¦quests§1033902Œ¥patchE¢id§1033902¢en¤Riol¢ja©ãƒªã‚ªãƒ«¢de¤Riol¢fr¤Riol¥title„¢en ¢ja ¢de ¢fr ¬defaultTalks¨position…¦zoneidÍá£mapÌˆ¡xË@ÌÌÌÌÌÍ¡yË@Që…¸R¡z␀¢ko¦ë¦¬ì˜¬¢zh©é‡Œå¥¥å°”¦quests§1033903Œ¥patchE¢id§1033903¢en­Hoary Boulder¢ja»ãƒ›ãƒ¼ãƒªãƒ¼ãƒ»ãƒœãƒ«ãƒ€ãƒ¼¢de­Grauer Felsen¢fr­Hoary Boulder¥title„¢en ¢ja ¢de ¢fr ¬defaultTalks¨position…¦zoneidÍá£mapÌˆ¡xË@záG®¡yË@£×
