=p¤¡y¡z␀¢ko¬ìœ„ë¦¬ì•™ì œ¢zh¬äºŽé‡Œæ˜‚çƒ­¦quests‘„¢idÎ␀â¤name„¢en¯Death Unto Dawn¢ja¯é»Žæ˜Žã®æ­»é—˜¢deµKampf im Morgengrauen¢fr°Aube meurtriÃ¨re¤icon´/i/071000/071201.png¦banner´/i/101000/101060.png§1036451Œ¥patchL¢id§1036451¢en¨Estinien¢jaµã‚¨ã‚¹ãƒ†ã‚£ãƒ‹ã‚¢ãƒ³¢de¨Estinien¢fr¨Estinien¥title„¢en ¢ja ¢de ¢fr ¬defaultTalks¨position…¦zoneidÍá£mapÌˆ¡xË@\(õÂ¡yË@õÂ\(ö¡z␀¢ko¯ì—ìŠ¤í‹°ë‹ˆì•™¢zh¯åŸƒæ–¯è’‚å°¼å®‰¦quests‘„¢idÎ␀â¤name„¢en¯Death Unto Dawn¢ja¯é»Žæ˜Žã®æ­»é—˜¢deµKampf im Morgengrauen¢fr°Aube meurtriÃ¨re¤icon´/i/071000/071201.png¦banner´/i/101000/101060.png§1036452Œ¥patchL¢id§1036452¢en©Alphinaud¢ja¯ã‚¢ãƒ«ãƒ•ã‚£ãƒŽ¢de©Alphinaud¢fr©Alphinaud¥title„¢en ¢ja ¢de ¢fr ¬defaultTalks‘’Ù•I have received word that Arenvald is back at the Phrontistery. As much as I would like to visit him, I shall wait until there is good news to share.ÙõThe last time we met, it was strange that he should be the one trying to cheer <i>me</i> up, in spite of everything that has befallen him. Still, I was glad for the chance to meet with him, and his words continue to be a source of encouragement.¨position…¦zoneidÍá£mapÌˆ¡xË@G®záH¡yË@Â\(õÃ¡z␀¢ko©ì•Œí”¼ë…¸¢zh¬é˜¿å°”è²è¯º¦quests‘…¢idÎ␀¤name„¢enµThe Next Ship to Sail¢jaÙ!ã‚„ãŒã¦æµã‚Œã¯æµ·ã¸ã¨æ³¨ã¢de¼Aufbruch zu neuen Horizonten¢fr¶Un pied devant l'autre¤icon´/i/071000/071201.png§rewards‘‚¢idÍ‹R¦amount¦banner´/i/101000/101098.png§1036453Œ¥patchL¢id§1036453¢en§Alisaie¢ja¬ã‚¢ãƒªã‚¼ãƒ¼¢de§Alisaie¢fr§Alisaie¥title„¢en ¢ja ¢de ¢fr ¬defaultTalks‘‘Ù]Whatever it is my father and the Forum are hiding, I'm determined to get to the bottom of it.¨position…¦zoneidÍá£mapÌˆ¡xË@ë…¸Qì¡yË@záG®{¡z␀¢ko©ì•Œë¦¬ì œ¢zh©é˜¿èŽ‰å¡ž¦quests§1036454Œ¥patchL¢id§1036454¢en¨Thancred¢ja²ã‚µãƒ³ã‚¯ãƒ¬ãƒƒãƒ‰¢de¨Thancred¢fr¨Thancred¥title„¢en ¢ja ¢de ¢fr ¬defaultTalks‘’ÚWhen Arenvald tried to free the Amalj'aa held in the tower, it triggered some sort of alarum and the captives were killed instantly. As such, we have no choice but to leave them in the clutches of the Telophoroi until a means of rescuing them has been found.ÙóIn the meantime, the summonings of lunar primals will continue. Just as we must rely on the Grand Company of Eorzea to put down such entities and prevent any further abductions, so too do they rely on us to come through with our investigation.¨position…¦zoneidÍá£mapÌˆ¡x¡yË@Â\(õÃ¡z␀¢ko¬ì‚°í¬ë ˆë“œ¢zh¬æ¡‘å…‹ç‘žå¾·¦quests§1036455Œ¥patchL¢id§1036455¢en¨Y'shtola¢ja²ãƒ¤ãƒ»ã‚·ãƒ¥ãƒˆãƒ©¢de¨Y'shtola¢fr¨Y'shtola¥title„¢en ¢ja ¢de ¢fr ¬defaultTalks‘’Ù¤Those who are brought within close proximity of the towers are tempered into serving Garlemald, then forced to summon lunar primals with aether drawn from the land.ÙºBut even having understood this, we are yet to uncover what the Telophoroi wish to achieve by all this. Are the towers purely for strategic advantage or do they serve some other purpose?¨position…¦zoneidÍá£mapÌˆ¡xË@ë…¸Qì¡yË@Që…¸R¡z␀¢ko¬ì•¼ìŠˆí†¨ë¼¢zh®é›…Â·ä¿®ç‰¹æ‹‰¦quests§1036456Œ¥patchL¢id§1036456¢en¨Urianger¢ja²ã‚¦ãƒªã‚¨ãƒ³ã‚¸ã‚§¢de¨Urianger¢fr¨Urianger¥title„¢en ¢ja ¢de ¢fr ¬defaultTalks‘‘ÚMuch and more have we discovered of the Telophoroi's machinations since Thancred and I did return from Garlemald. Verily, their troops doth appear to have been tempered in much the same manner as those engaged in the construction of the towering edifice in the capital.¨position…¦zoneidÍá£mapÌˆ¡xË@õÂ\(ö¡yË@áG®zá¡z␀¢ko¬ìœ„ë¦¬ì•™ì œ¢zh¬äºŽé‡Œæ˜‚çƒ­¦quests§1036457Œ¥patchL¢id§1036457¢enªG'raha Tia¢ja¸ã‚°ãƒ»ãƒ©ãƒãƒ»ãƒ†ã‚£ã‚¢¢deªG'raha Tia¢frªG'raha Tia¥title„¢en ¢ja ¢de ¢fr ¬defaultTalks‘’ÚNNot only do the members of the Forum intend to adhere to their long-standing policy of nonintervention, they made a point of sending Master Fourchenault here to explicitly state that fact. Rather than simply refusing to involve themselves in our affairs, it would appear they are actively trying to prevent us from meddling in theirs.Ù›That does, of course, make Krile's mission of securing our entry i